{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '80,90p' paper.tex; sed -n '950,990p' source_evidence/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '848,865p' source_evidence/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '1,70p' source_evidence/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '101,166p' build_artifacts.py; cat literature/retrieve_approved.py\"","aggregated_output":"For a pair $(a,b)\\in\\{0,\\ldots,p-1\\}^2$, the target is either $(a+b)\\bmod p$ or $(a-b)\\bmod p$, with $p=97$. Each operation has $p^2=9,409$ possible ordered pairs. The final evaluation uses a deterministic subset of 4,705 pairs for each operation, with 1,411 training pairs and 3,294 held-out pairs. Thus the training set is approximately 30\\% of the retained subset, not 30\\% of the entire operation table; it covers approximately 15\\% of all possible inputs. Addition and subtraction use independently constructed operation-specific partitions.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L588-L613]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/final/benchmark.json]]\n\nThe partition is reproducible without downloading data. Each input and operation are encoded in canonical JSON, normalized, and hashed. Sorting the hashes separates the development subset from the final subset. A second hash ordering with a fixed training prefix assigns the training portion within the final subset. The split is fixed across initialization seeds and widths. Consequently, seed variability measures training-initialization variability on a fixed split, not uncertainty over fresh data partitions. The held-out set is used for recording performance, not for gradient updates. Appendix~\\ref{app:construction} specifies the construction and readable source locations.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L588-L631]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L825-L870]]\n\nWe report both operations rather than treating subtraction as an unseen transfer task. Each network is independently trained from scratch on its own operation. The shared architecture and optimization recipe permit a condition-specific replication of the width comparison, but not a claim of cross-task representation transfer.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n            training = [[row[\"a\"], row[\"b\"], row[\"label\"]] for row in rows if row[\"split\"] == \"train\"]\n            heldout = [[row[\"a\"], row[\"b\"], row[\"label\"]] for row in rows if row[\"split\"] == \"heldout\"]\n            if smoke:\n                training, heldout = training[:128], heldout[:256]\n            def train_call(request):\n                nonlocal baseline_failure\n                try:\n                    return worker.call(request, timeout=max(.001, method_deadline - time.monotonic()))\n                except RequiredBaselineFailure as failure:\n                    baseline_failure = failure.category\n                    raise\n            current_operation = \"baseline_worker\"\n            trace = [train_call({\"op\": \"init\", **episode, \"train\": training, \"test\": heldout, \"horizon\": horizon})]\n            for step in range(0, horizon, block_steps):\n                category = worker.failure_category()\n                if category:\n                    baseline_failure = category\n                    raise RequiredBaselineFailure(category)\n                response = call({\"op\": \"schedule\", \"step\": step, \"steps\": horizon, \"block_steps\": block_steps})\n                expected = max(.0001, min(.01, normalized[0] * normalized[1] ** (step / horizon)))\n                if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {\"lr\"} or not finite_number(response[\"lr\"]) or not .0001 <= response[\"lr\"] <= .01 or not math.isclose(response[\"lr\"], expected, rel_tol=0, abs_tol=1e-12):\n                    raise ProtocolError(\"invalid_schedule\")\n                if time.monotonic() >= method_deadline:\n                    raise TimeoutError()\n                trace.append(train_call({\"op\": \"train\", \"lr\": response[\"lr\"], \"steps\": block_steps}))\n            if trace[-1][\"step\"] != horizon or len(trace) != horizon // block_steps + 1:\n                raise RequiredBaselineFailure(\"baseline_result_failure\")\n            return summarize_trace(trace, horizon)\n\n        outcomes, complete = run_declared_episodes(episodes, hard_deadline=hard_deadline,\n            finish_reserve=finish_reserve, reset_timeout=1 if smoke else 10,\n            episode_overhead=4, rpc_cap=1 if smoke else 15,\n            clock=time.monotonic, rpc=candidate.call, evaluate=evaluate_episode,\n            worst_case=lambda episode: worst_case(episode, horizon), record_failure=record_failure,\n            outcomes=outcomes)\n        if time.monotonic() >= hard_deadline - finish_reserve:\n            complete = False\n    except Exception as failure:\n        error = failure\n        complete = False\n    finally:\n            if sum(parameter.numel() for parameter in model.parameters()) != 292 * width + 97:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"invalid_architecture\")\n            response = checkpoint()\n        elif request[\"op\"] == \"train\":\n            if state[\"step\"] + request[\"steps\"] > state[\"horizon\"]:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"update_budget_exceeded\")\n            for group in state[\"optimizer\"].param_groups:\n                group[\"lr\"] = request[\"lr\"]\n            for _ in range(request[\"steps\"]):\n                state[\"optimizer\"].zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n                loss = functional.cross_entropy(state[\"model\"](state[\"train_x\"]), state[\"train_y\"])\n                loss.backward()\n                state[\"optimizer\"].step()\n                state[\"step\"] += 1\n            response = checkpoint()\n        else:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"unknown_worker_operation\")\n        sys.stdout.buffer.write(bounded_json_line(response))\n\"\"\"Self-contained CPU neural factorial evaluator; no candidate-reported science.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport resource\nimport selectors\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport statistics\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\n\nPLANE = \"final\"\nSEEDS = [1009, 2027, 3037]\nWALL_SECONDS = 64800\nRPC_BUDGET = 1512\nSTART = time.monotonic()\nWIRE_LIMIT = 64 * 1024 * 1024\nAPPLICATION_LIMIT = 16384\nCONTROLS = (\"constant\", \"copy\", \"deranged\", \"initial\")\nFINAL_METRICS = (\"combined_score\", \"correct\", \"completion_fraction\", \"delayed_fraction\",\n                 \"restricted_mean_lag\", \"width_lag_contrast\", \"decay_interaction\",\n                 \"width_lag_ci_low\", \"width_lag_ci_high\", \"control_gap\")\n\n\nclass InvalidResetResponse(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef require_reset_ack(response):\n    if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {\"ok\"} or response[\"ok\"] is not True:\n        raise InvalidResetResponse(\"invalid reset response\")\n\n\ndef bounded_failure_name(value, fallback):\n    import re\n    return value if isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,79}\", value) else fallback\n\n\nclass RequiredBaselineFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"invalid_baseline_diagnostic\")\n        super().__init__(\"required baseline failed\")\n\n\nclass ProtocolError(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category=\"malformed_response\"):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"malformed_response\")\n        super().__init__(self.category)\n\n\nclass BrokerTransportFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, operation):\n        self.operation = bounded_failure_name(operation, \"unknown\")\n        super().__init__(\"broker_transport_failure\")\n\n\ndef describe_episode_failure(error, operation):\n    context = error\n    for _ in range(8):\n        if isinstance(context, BrokerTransportFailure):\n            return {\"component\": \"broker\", \"category\": \"broker_transport_failure\",\n                          \"memorization\": [row[\"memorization\"] for row in rows],\n                          \"generalization_count\": sum(row[\"generalization\"] is not None for row in rows),\n                          \"mean_train_percent\": 100 * statistics.fmean(row[\"late_train\"] for row in rows),\n                          \"mean_heldout_percent\": 100 * statistics.fmean(row[\"late_heldout\"] for row in rows),\n                          \"sd_heldout_percent\": 100 * statistics.stdev(row[\"late_heldout\"] for row in rows),\n                          \"mean_lag\": statistics.fmean(row[\"lag\"] for row in rows)})\n    contrasts = {}\n    for decay in (0, 1):\n        contrasts[decay] = [statistics.fmean(next(row[\"lag\"] for row in records if row[\"seed\"] == seed and row[\"operation\"] == operation and row[\"decay\"] == decay and row[\"width\"] == 16)\n                               - next(row[\"lag\"] for row in records if row[\"seed\"] == seed and row[\"operation\"] == operation and row[\"decay\"] == decay and row[\"width\"] == 256)\n                               for operation in OPERATIONS) for seed in seeds]\n    metrics = paper_data[\"final_evaluation\"][\"metrics\"]\n    assert statistics.fmean(contrasts[1]) == metrics[\"width_lag_contrast\"]\n    assert abs(statistics.fmean(contrasts[1]) - statistics.fmean(contrasts[0]) - metrics[\"decay_interaction\"]) < 1e-10\n    assert abs(statistics.fmean(row[\"lag\"] for row in records) - metrics[\"restricted_mean_lag\"]) < 1e-10\n    derived = {\"seeds\": seeds, \"records\": records, \"conditions\": summaries, \"paired_contrasts\": contrasts,\n               \"memorization_count\": sum(row[\"memorization\"] is not None for row in records),\n               \"generalization_count\": sum(row[\"generalization\"] is not None for row in records),\n               \"complete_count\": sum(row[\"complete\"] for row in records),\n               \"horizon\": horizon, \"overall_heldout_percent\": 100 * statistics.fmean(row[\"late_heldout\"] for row in records),\n               \"control_means_percent\": {name: 100 * statistics.fmean(row[\"controls\"][name] for row in records) for name in records[0][\"controls\"]},\n               \"duration_seconds_by_seed\": {episode[\"seed\"]: episode[\"duration_seconds\"] for episode in episodes}}\n    write_output(\"analysis/derived_results.json\", json.dumps(derived, indent=2) + \"\\n\", \"derived\")\n\n    heading = r\"Operation & $\\lambda$ & Width & \" + \" & \".join(f\"$T_M^{{({seed})}}$\" for seed in seeds) + r\" & $G$ observed \\\\\"\n    event_lines = [\"% \" + EPISODE_REF, r\"\\begin{tabular}{llrrrrr}\", r\"\\toprule\", heading, r\"\\midrule\"]\n    for entry in summaries:\n        values = [r\"\\textemdash\" if value is None else f\"{value:,}\" for value in entry[\"memorization\"]]\n        event_lines.append(f\"{entry['operation'].capitalize()} & {entry['decay']} & {entry['width']} & \" + \" & \".join(values) + f\" & {entry['generalization_count']}/3 \" + r\"\\\\\")\n    event_lines.extend([r\"\\bottomrule\", r\"\\end{tabular}\"])\n    write_output(\"tables/events.tex\", \"\\n\".join(event_lines) + \"\\n\", \"table\")\n\n    full_lines = [\"% \" + EPISODE_REF, r\"\\begin{longtable}{llrrrrrr}\", r\"\\toprule\", r\"Op. & $\\lambda$ & Width & Seed & $T_M$ & $L_H$ & Train (\\%) & Held-out (\\%) \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\\endhead\"]\n    for row in sorted(records, key=lambda entry: (entry[\"operation\"], entry[\"decay\"], entry[\"width\"], entry[\"seed\"])):\n        value = r\"\\textemdash\" if row[\"memorization\"] is None else str(row[\"memorization\"])\n        full_lines.append(f\"{row['operation'][:3]}. & {row['decay']} & {row['width']} & {row['seed']} & {value} & {row['lag']} & {100*row['late_train']:.3f} & {100*row['late_heldout']:.3f} \" + r\"\\\\\")\n    full_lines.extend([r\"\\bottomrule\", r\"\\end{longtable}\"])\n    write_output(\"tables/full_observations.tex\", \"\\n\".join(full_lines) + \"\\n\", \"table\")\n\n    diagnostic_lines = [\"% \" + EPISODE_REF, r\"\\begin{tabular}{llrrrr}\", r\"\\toprule\", r\"Op. & $\\lambda$ & Width & Train CE & Held-out CE & Weight norm \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\"]\n    for (operation, decay, width), rows in grouped.items():\n        values = [statistics.fmean(row[key] for row in rows) for key in (\"final_train_loss\", \"final_heldout_loss\", \"final_norm\")]\n        diagnostic_lines.append(f\"{operation.capitalize()} & {decay} & {width} & \" + \" & \".join(f\"{value:.3g}\" for value in values) + r\" \\\\\")\n    diagnostic_lines.extend([r\"\\bottomrule\", r\"\\end{tabular}\"])\n    write_output(\"tables/diagnostics.tex\", \"\\n\".join(diagnostic_lines) + \"\\n\", \"table\")\n\n    plt.rcParams.update({\"font.family\": \"DejaVu Sans\", \"font.size\": 13.5, \"axes.titlesize\": 14,\n                         \"axes.labelsize\": 13.5, \"xtick.labelsize\": 13.5, \"ytick.labelsize\": 13.5,\n                         \"legend.fontsize\": 13.5, \"pdf.fonttype\": 42, \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n                         \"axes.spines.right\": False, \"axes.linewidth\": .8})\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(8.25, 5.15), sharex=True, sharey=\"row\")\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.13, right=.98, top=.84, bottom=.14, hspace=.28, wspace=.13)\n    for column, operation in enumerate(OPERATIONS):\n        for row_index, metric in enumerate((\"late_train\", \"late_heldout\")):\n            axis = axes[row_index, column]\n            for decay in (0, 1):\n                for width_index, width in enumerate(widths):\n                    rows = grouped[(operation, decay, width)]\n                    xcenter = width_index + (-.12 if decay == 0 else .12)\n                    values = [100 * row[metric] for row in rows]\n                    for seed_index, value in enumerate(values):\n                        axis.plot(xcenter + (seed_index-1)*.035, value, marker=(\"o\", \"s\", \"^\")[seed_index], color=DECAY_COLORS[decay], ms=5, ls=\"none\", alpha=.85)\n                    axis.plot([xcenter-.075, xcenter+.075], [statistics.fmean(values)]*2, lw=2, color=DECAY_COLORS[decay])\n            axis.set_xticks(range(len(widths)), [str(width) for width in widths])\n            axis.set_xlim(-.4, 2.4)\n            axis.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=.18)\nimport hashlib\nimport html\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport requests\n\nAPPROVED = [\n    (\"2201.02177\", \"Power2022GrokkingGB\"),\n    (\"1711.05101\", \"Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD\"),\n    (\"2210.01117\", \"Liu2023Omnigrok\"),\n    (\"2309.02390\", \"Varma2023ExplainingGT\"),\n    (\"2310.06110\", \"Kumar2024LazyRich\"),\n    (\"2303.06173\", \"Davies2023Unifying\"),\n    (\"1912.02292\", \"Nakkiran2020DoubleDescent\"),\n    (\"1611.03530\", \"Zhang2017Rethinking\"),\n]\n\n\ndef clean(text):\n    return html.unescape(re.sub(r\"<[^>]+>\", \"\", text)).strip()\n\n\ndef retrieve():\n    references = []\n    entries = []\n    for identifier, citation_key in APPROVED:\n        url = f\"https://arxiv.org/abs/{identifier}\"\n        response = requests.get(url, timeout=60)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        document = response.text\n        metadata = {}\n        for name, value in re.findall(r'<meta\\s+name=\"([^\"]+)\"\\s+content=\"([^\"]*)\"', document):\n            metadata.setdefault(name, []).append(html.unescape(value))\n        title = metadata[\"citation_title\"][0]\n        authors = metadata[\"citation_author\"]\n        abstract_match = re.search(r'<blockquote class=\"abstract[^>]*>(.*?)</blockquote>', document, re.S)\n        abstract = clean(abstract_match.group(1)).removeprefix(\"Abstract:\").strip()\n        text = f\"Title: {title}\\nAuthors: {'; '.join(authors)}\\nSource: {url}\\n\\nAbstract consulted:\\n{abstract}\\n\"\n        path = Path(f\"literature/{identifier}.txt\")\n        path.write_text(text)\n        year = metadata[\"citation_date\"][0].split(\"/\")[0].split(\"-\")[0]\n        entries.append(\"@article{\" + citation_key + \",\\n  title={\" + title + \"},\\n  author={\" + \" and \".join(authors) + \"},\\n  year={\" + year + \"},\\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:\" + identifier + \"},\\n  url={\" + url + \"}\\n}\\n\")\n        references.append({\"id\": \"ref.arxiv.\" + identifier, \"citation_key\": citation_key, \"title\": title,\n                           \"source_url\": url, \"year\": int(year), \"retrieved_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n                           \"consulted_scope\": \"Title, authors, and abstract only; no citation graph or recommendations read\",\n                           \"local_path\": str(path), \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})\n    Path(\"references.bib\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(entries))\n    Path(\"references_provenance.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"count\": len(references), \"references\": references,\n        \"safety_boundary\": \"Only the eight exact identities approved by paper_strategy and the task starter list\",\n        \"minimum_reference_count_unmet\": True}, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    retrieve()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
